<!--Post: 12794--><!--Time: 1113246138-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12794"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 12:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Reporting at Ks.com that the Radinator may have tried to terminate his pitiful existence. Report comes from ksn.com.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12794-->
<!--Post: 12795--><!--Time: 1113246555-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12795"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 12:09 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To add to that - if he did, it would be a travesty. He would have maintained control to the very end and cheated the justice system. I do hope he&#39;s prevented from offing himself before he can hopefully suffer a violent death at the hands of someone in the same mindset as the dude who beat Dahmer to death.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12795-->
<!--Post: 12796--><!--Time: 1113248476-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12796"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 12:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ll bet he doesn&#39;t even know the case against him is about to get a whole lot WEAKER. <BR> <BR>I wasn&#39;t gonna come back for a while but when I found out more gross WPD bungling, I had to speak out. Ask NOLA or the CHIEF or CITY ATTORNEY who draws up warrants about this....It&#39;s called a HIPPA warrant. Evidently the WPD FAILED to secure one before getting his daughters DNA sample which in turn nailed Dennis and led to the gathering of a lot of info. It might just go into the toilet now <BR>The 4th Amendment protects us from &#34;unreasonable search and seizure.&#34;Additionally, HIPPA regulations federally protect the privacy of our medical records. However, it is possible for prosecutors to get those medical records but they must follow very specific procedures for the evidence to hold up in court. Failure to follow HIPPA regulations in obtaining Rader’s daughters’ DNA could allow the case to be thrown out. <BR> <BR>Now, you MAY have other info that MIGHT help convict him but as far as Dee Davis and Marine Hedge I should imagine their families won&#39;t be too thrilled to hear this. ANYTHING cops sniffed out or recovered AFTER the daughters DNA is at severe risk right now. <BR> <BR>That awards ceremony on that Saturday Morning looks worse and worse....<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12796-->
<!--Post: 12800--><!--Time: 1113252356-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12800"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 1:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh boy Steve, NOW you&#39;ve done it. You&#39;ve actually made WPD deny this rumor. They&#39;ll be kicking down your door any minute for making them do something. They said it &#40;suicide attempt&#41; didn&#39;t happen on Kansas.com and here is the last paragraph: <BR> <BR>Rader was arrested on Feb. 25 in his hometown of Park City. His preliminary hearing is scheduled for April 19 in Sedgwick County District Court. The rumor about a suicide attempt had surfaced on a BTK online discussion board. <BR> <BR> <BR>Ummmmm, you&#39;re gonna get SO grounded<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12800-->
<!--Post: 12801--><!--Time: 1113254469-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12801"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 2:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A psychopath attempts to commit suicide to maintain domination and control. Dennis Rader is not accustomed to a subservient role. He enjoyed informing neighbors of minor infractions of local council codes and primarily murdering women in their homes. He does not appreciate law enforcement dictating his life and incarcerating him. Suicide symbolizes his last attempt to control the direction of his life.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12801-->
<!--Post: 12805--><!--Time: 1113273976-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12805"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, April 11, 2005 - 7:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Heeeeee.....Yeah, EYES actually started the whole ball rolling. I have learned yet another lesson in considering the m&#42;&#42;&#42;erf&#42;&#42;&#42;ing source.  <BR> <BR>However, I did get to make the worthwhile point, as re-stated in a far more elegant manner by Ivy Leaguer, that were Rader to have done this, it would have only been an act of control. Psychopaths don&#39;t kill themselves out of depression. They do it to stay large and in charge.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12805-->
